{"name":"Bypass","hex":"#b6c4d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bypass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A road that passes around something, such as a residential area or business district.","A replacement road for obsolete road that is no longer in use because devastating natural disasters (earthquakes, tsunamis, landslides)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To avoid an obstacle etc, by constructing or using a bypass.","To ignore the usual channels or procedures."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bypass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bypass (road)","blocks":[{"text":"A bypass is a road or highway that avoids or \"bypasses\" a built-up area, town, or village, to let through traffic flow without interference from local traffic, to reduce congestion in the built-up area, to improve road safety and as replacement for obsolete roads that are no longer in use as a result of devastating natural disasters. A bypass specifically designated for trucks may be called a truck route."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Nasinneula_nakyma_1.jpg/330px-Nasinneula_nakyma_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bypass_(road)","wikidata":"Q1779930"},{"title":"Flood bypass","blocks":[{"text":"A flood bypass is a region of land or a large man-made structure that is designed to convey excess flood waters from a river or stream in order to reduce the risk of flooding on the natural river or stream near a key point of interest, such as a city. Flood bypasses, sometimes called floodways, often have man-made diversion works, such as diversion weirs and spillways, at their head or point of origin. The main body of a flood bypass is often a natural flood plain. Many flood bypasses are designed to carry enough water such that combined flows down the original river or stream and flood bypass will not exceed the expected maximum flood flow of the river or stream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Normal_floods_in_Weimar-Roth%2C_Germany_Flutmulde_of_river_Lahn_2015-12-02.JPG/330px-Normal_floods_in_Weimar-Roth%2C_Germany_Flutmulde_of_river_Lahn_2015-12-02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flood_bypass","wikidata":"Q5460060"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_A34%2C_Donnington.jpg/330px-The_A34%2C_Donnington.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_A34%2C_Donnington.jpg/330px-The_A34%2C_Donnington.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Newbury bypass near Donnington","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_A34%2C_Donnington.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/149ea452.jpg/500px-149ea452.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/149ea452.jpg/500px-149ea452.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old by-pass sign on Maui for State Route 30 thru surface streets","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A149ea452.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Interstate_95_-_Virginia_%288112215303%29.jpg/500px-Interstate_95_-_Virginia_%288112215303%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Interstate_95_-_Virginia_%288112215303%29.jpg/1280px-Interstate_95_-_Virginia_%288112215303%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Interstate_95_-_Virginia_%288112215303%29.jpg/500px-Interstate_95_-_Virginia_